    "description": "Earned a full scholarship to Project Underdog's bootcamp, where I studied software engineering full-time, paired 1:1 with industry professionals. (https://www.underdogdevs.org/)\n\nSome of my work includes:\n\n•Carpooly: JavaScript/Express/NoSQL - Gathered a team of four peers around Carpooly, an app that makes it easy to split the costs of carpooling. Act as tech lead. Manage stand ups and help define tasks for each team member. Improved developer productivity by establishing GitHub branch protections, implementing hot module reload, and writing the README for our project.\n\n•Texas Holdem: HTML/CSS/JavaScript - This is a fun project for a Texas Holdem style poker game. I used vanilla JavaScript, HTML, and CSS to build the UI and the logic.\nDemo: https://kensonjohnson.github.io/texas-holdem/\nSource: https://github.com/kensonjohnson/texas-holdem",
